Time Complexity: O(log² n), because we perform binary search in a range of size up to 5 × n, which takes O(log n) steps. In each step, we compute the number of trailing zeroes using Legendre’s formula, which takes another O(log n) time due to repeated division by 5.Auxiliary Space: O(1), The algorithm uses a constant amount of extra space—just a few integer variables for binary search and counting. No recursion, arrays, or additional data structures are used.
